police say they will not charge a  Florida man for killing another man in a  parking lot after an argument  surveillance video shows Michael Draco  was pushed over by Marquis McLaughlin  and responded with a single gun shot  Florida's Stand Your Ground law allows  people to respond with deadly force when  they believe their lives are in danger  protestors gathered at the scene  yesterday demanding justice for  mclaughlin Nagala burr who's in  clearwater florida spoke to his  girlfriend meg good morning  John good morning as you can see there's  a small memorial outside the store for  McLaughlin the family had parked in this  handicapped spot McLaughlin took his  five-year-old son II inside to buy  snacks less than three minutes later he  was gunned down for parking here  illegally he just tried to protect me  his kids  Brittany Jacob saw her boyfriend of nine  years Marquis McLaughlin shot and killed  in front of her last Thursday they went  to a convenience store with their three  children  McLaughlin walked inside with their  five-year-old son that's when Michael  Drake approached Jacobs  she says he berated her for parking in a  handicap spot without a permit do you  wanted me to you know move my car but  you know I had my right to party  anywhere I want to park surveillance but  it shows McLaughlin walk out of the  store in shoved rekha to the ground  seconds later Drake up pulled out his  gun and fired a single shot into  McLaughlin's chest the 28 year old  stumbled back into the store and  collapsed in front of his son what did  he take from you  my soul you know my partner you know we  did everything together no Drake ax has  a concealed weapons permit and told  police he shot McLaughlin because he  feared for his life  the Sheriff's Office says he is  protected by Florida's Stand Your Ground  law which allows people to use deadly  force when fearing imminent death or  great bodily harm without a duty to try  to escape the danger he had to shoot to  defend himself you know and those are  the facts and that's the law  but Jacob says McLaughlin backed away  from Drake after he pushed him this is  wrong because all my man was trying to  do is protect his girl like anybody else  would  the couple's four month old son in three  year old daughter were inside the car  during the shooting Jacobs told me that  she learned Drake ax wouldn't be charged  from the news CBS News has not been able  to reach Drake up for comment the State  Attorney's Office will have the final  say on whether to press charges  gaile all right thank you very much meg
 

